### :: Test case for issue #7202: when no package name can be found in its opam
### :: file, a pinned archive should be named after the archive
### OPAMYES=1
### opam switch create archive-pin-noname --empty
### <pin:archive-pin/opam>
opam-version: "2.0"
### tar czf archive-pin.tgz archive-pin
### opam pin ./archive-pin.tgz -n
[NOTE] Package archive-pin does not exist in opam repositories registered in the current switch.
archive-pin is now pinned to file://${BASEDIR}/archive-pin.tgz (version dev)
### opam pin
archive-pin.dev  (uninstalled)  rsync  file://${BASEDIR}/archive-pin.tgz
